{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph whose vertices and edges sit at integer positions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexPositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgePositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":", with possible holes."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/sparselyindexeddirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" describe dense indices with no holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and keep their laws. A conformer reports them only while it has no holes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Algorithms use this refinement to number the live vertices and edges with arrays while holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exist, instead of hashing every vertex and edge they meet. The bounds are upper bounds only.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed out, and nothing in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the library allocates by it. Position-keyed state goes through a paged map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"_PositionNumbers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), O(live elements + pages).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexPositionBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexPosition(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex(atPosition:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are inverses, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgePositionBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists in increasing order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without holes, the bounds equal "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and positions are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_numberedRows(outward:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" numbers the live vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lists, for each number, the numbers of its successors (outward) or predecessors, with the edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions beside them, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols023SparselyIndexedDirectedA0P","roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Sparsely